## 6. Terraform File Structure

```
CloudFront/
├── main.tf          # data sources, OAC, distribution, bucket policy
├── providers.tf     # terraform block, aws provider (region = var.aws_region), backend (commented)
├── variables.tf     # aws_region, environment, bucket_name, comment, price_class, tags
├── outputs.tf       # distribution_id, distribution_arn, distribution_domain_name
└── Vars/
    ├── us-east-2/
    │   ├── dev.tfvars   # REAL values — content-public bucket, ready to apply
    │   ├── uat.tfvars   # placeholder (bucket_name TBD, migration pending)
    │   └── prd.tfvars   # placeholder (bucket_name TBD)
    └── us-east-1/
        ├── dev.tfvars   # placeholder — only if a us-east-1 origin exists, or when
        │                #   adding a custom domain (ACM must live in us-east-1)
        ├── uat.tfvars   # placeholder
        └── prd.tfvars   # placeholder
```

Single root config, driven by per-region/env var-files. Only `Vars/us-east-2/dev.tfvars`
has real values; the rest are placeholders with `bucket_name` commented out so they can't
be run half-configured.

**Variables:** `aws_region` (required), `environment` (required), `bucket_name` (required),
`comment` (default ""), `price_class` (default `PriceClass_100`), `tags` (default {}).

